<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμν-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίμνη</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>from the
				marsh</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνιθας χερσαίους καὶ
			λ.</span> both land-fowl and <i>water</i>-fowl, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.119
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				272
			</span></i>; of the crocodile, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὸν . . τετράπουν, χερσαῖον καὶ λ.
					ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.68
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. κρηνῶν τέκνα</span>, of frogs,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				211
			</span></i>; of the beaver, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				307
			</span></i>; of an eel, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				8.355d
			</span></i> (vulg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμνία</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> λ. φυτόν</span>
			<i>water</i>-plant, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.399f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of water,
				<i>stagnant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for marshes</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ.
				πλοῖον, σκάφος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.317.9
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				1.31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἄνεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λίμναι</span>) <i>of</i> or <i>from Limnae</i>, epith. of
			Dionysus, from his temple there, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				37
			</span></i> P.: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιμναῖον, τό</span>, <i>a temple of Artemis at
			Limnae</i>, on the borders of Laconia and Messenia, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.4.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				3.2.6
			</span></i>: hence she was called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιμνᾶτις</span></b> 
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμνήτης</span>
			; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιμναία</span></b> ,
			epith. of Artemis at Sicyon and elsewhere, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.7.6
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
